-- title:
--   Level automorphisms over L for γ∈Γ₀(M')
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q\ge 5$, let $M'\ge 1$ with $q\nmid M'$, and let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell\ge 3$, $\ell\ne q$ and $\ell\nmid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero, $\xi\in L$ a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity, and assume there is at least one ring homomorphism $\iota:L\to\mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\xi)=e^{2\pi i/(q\ell)}$. Let $H=\ker\bigl((\mathbb{Z}/(q\ell)^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb{Z}/q\ell)^\times\bigr)$, and let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L\subseteq L((X))$ equal to `laurentBaseChange`, i.e. the $L$-subfield of $L((X))$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the field `xHFunctionField` of $q$-expansions attached to $\Gamma_H((q\ell)^2M')$ under $\mathbb{Q}((X))\to L((X))$. Then for every $\gamma\in\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ lying in $\Gamma_0(M')$ there exists an $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ satisfying `IsLevelAutAt` for $\gamma^{-1}$: for every weight $k$, every pair of modular forms $f,g$ of weight $k$ on $\Gamma_H((q\ell)^2M')$ admitting integral power series $p_f,p_g$ whose images in $\mathbb{C}[[X]]$ are the $q$-expansions (width $1$) of $f,g$, with $p_g$ nonzero over $\mathbb{Q}$, every $x\in K$ equal to the image of $p_f/p_g$, and every $\iota:L\to\mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\xi)=e^{2\pi i/(q\ell)}$, one has $\iota(\tau x)\cdot q\text{-exp}(g\mid_k\gamma^{-\sharp})=q\text{-exp}(f\mid_k\gamma^{-\sharp})$ in $\mathbb{C}((X))$, where $\gamma^{-\sharp}=\mathrm{diag}(q\ell,1)^{-1}\gamma^{-1}\mathrm{diag}(q\ell,1)$ is `conjElemN`.
--
--   This is the statement that the action of $\Gamma_0(M')$ on the function field of the full-level curve $X(\Gamma(q\ell)\cap\Gamma_0(M'))$ by pull-back is realised by automorphisms defined over the coefficient field $L$ containing $\mu_{q\ell}$, in the form of Shimura's theory of canonical models. It is the source of the level automorphisms used throughout the subsequent analysis of the auxiliary-level curve, in particular in the study of blow-up charts and of the Galois action on their fibres.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_AuxLevel_exists_isLevelAutAt_of_mem_gamma0_of_exists_ringHom.lean

